! The three BRANCH-ON-BIT variants nothing drove: BZB1, BZBN, BZBZ.
!
! HOW THEY WERE FOUND.  audit_opcode_coverage.py screens every mnemonic
! STRAP can emit against every program.  Of the 22 unused, 15 are
! documented scope limits that reach setOpInvalid; seven are IMPLEMENTED
! and simply undriven.  These are three of the seven.
!
! WHAT IS NEW.  bb_branch_on_bit.strap and bb_indicator.strap drive the
! branch-IF-ON half of the family (BB, BB1, BBZ, BBN).  The branch-IF-OFF
! half with a modifier -- BZB1, BZBN, BZBZ -- had no coverage at all.
! BZB itself is used widely; it is the three that also CHANGE the bit
! that were missing.
!
! THE MODIFIER TABLE, Reference Manual p.41 and the X22-6533 pocket card
! ("Branch when bit tested matches"): instruction bits 60-61 give
! 00 unchanged, 01 set to zero, 10 inverted, 11 set to one, and bit 62
! selects branch-if-on (BB*) or branch-if-off (BZB*).
!
! THE RULE THIS BLOCK REALLY PINS is the one that is easy to get wrong:
! "WHETHER OR NOT the branch was taken, the tested bit is set" (p.41).
! Step 2 below is that case on its own -- the bit is ON, so a BZBN does
! NOT branch, and it must still be inverted.  A model that only applied
! the modifier on the taken path would pass steps 1 and 3 and fail step
! 2.
!
! WEAKER STANDARD, STATED: hand-written from p.41, not transcribed.  No
! deck block found so far uses a branch-if-off form with a modifier.

        SLC, (8)2600.0
!
! ---- step 1: bit off -> BZB1 branches, and sets the bit to one ------
START   BZB1, SCR, T1                ! off: branch taken, bit := 1
        BEW, $                       ! hang up: BZB1 should have branched
T1      BZB, SCR, $                  ! hang up if bit off -- it must be 1 now
!
! ---- step 2: bit on -> BZBN does NOT branch, and still inverts ------
        BZBN, SCR, NOBR              ! on: no branch, but bit := inverted
        BB, SCR, $                   ! hang up if bit on -- invert must have
                                     !   happened on the NOT-taken path
!
! ---- step 3: bit off -> BZBZ branches, and leaves it zero -----------
        BZBZ, SCR, T3                ! off: branch taken, bit := 0
        BEW, $                       ! hang up: BZBZ should have branched
T3      BB, SCR, $                   ! hang up if bit on -- must still be 0
        B, PASS
!
NOBR    BEW, $                       ! hang up: BZBN branched on a bit that
                                     !   was ON, and BZB* branches if OFF
SCR     DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! the scratch word; bit 0 is the target
PASS    BEW, $
        END, START
